{
  "title": "Hip Labral Tear",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3097/hip-labral-tear",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Mar 25 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A hip labral tear is a traumatic tear of the acetabular labrum, mostly common seen in acetabular dysplasia, that may lead to symptoms of internal snapping hip as well hip locking with hip range of motion.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis generally requires an MR arthrogram of the hip joint in question.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is a nonoperative trial to include NSAIDs, rest and physical therapy. Arthroscopic labral debridement versus repair is indicated for patients with progressive symptoms who failed nonoperative management.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "highest incidence in patients with **acetabular dysplasia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "seen in all age groups",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "patients commonly **active females**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**anterosuperior labrum** most common location",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**femoroacetabular impingement**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**hip dysplasia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "floppy labrum more susceptible to tearing",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**trauma**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "hip dislocations/subluxations are a common cause",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**capsular laxity**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "increased translational forces across labrum due to joint hypermobility",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**joint degeneration**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "causes acetabular edge loading",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Structure",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "horse-shoe shaped structure **continuous with transverse acetabular ligament**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3097/images/labrum%20body.jpg",
                  "caption": "cadaver labrum"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "2 parts",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "articular",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "fibrocartilage",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "capsular",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "dense connective tissue",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Vascularity",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "capsule and synovium at acetabular margin",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**only peripheral 1/3rd of the labrum is vascularized**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Innervation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**highly innervated** with mechanoreceptors and nocioreceptors",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "branch of nerve to the quadratus femoris",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "obturator nerve",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanical hip **pain** and **snapping**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may have vague groin pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may be associated with a sensation of **locking**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "provocative tests",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "anterior labral tear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "pain if hip is brought from a fully flexed, externally rotated, and abducted position to a position of extension, internal rotation, and adduction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "posterior labral tear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "pain if hip is brought from a flexed, adducted, and internally rotated position to one of abduction, external rotation, and extension.",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "useful to exclude other types of hip pathology",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may show",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "hip dysplasia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "arthritis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "acetabular cysts",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**MRI arthrogram**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3097/images/mri%20arthrogram.jpg",
              "caption": "MRI arthrogram"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "imaging study of choice",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "92% sensitive for detecting labral tears",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "may be combined with **intra-articular injections of lidocaine and steroid** for diagnostic and therapeutic purposes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rest, NSAIDS, physical therapy, steroid injections",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "initial treatment of choice for all patients with labral tears",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "no long-term follow-up data on conservative management",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "arthroscopic labral debridement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "symptoms that have failed to improve with nonoperative modalities",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "labral tear not amenable to repair",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "remove any unstable portions of the labrum and associated synovitis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "underlying hip pathology (e.g. FAI) should also be addressed at time of surgery",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "post-operative care",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "limited weight-bearing x4 weeks",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "flexion and abduction are limited for 4 to 6 weeks",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "70-85% experience short-term relief of symptoms following arthroscopic debridement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "long-term follow-up data not available",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "arthroscopic labral repair",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**indications**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**symptoms that have failed to improve with nonoperative modalities**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "full-thickness tears at the labral-chondral junction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "unknown at this time",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "labral reconstruction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "symptoms that have failed to improve with nonoperative modalities, with an irreparable labrum",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "allograft and autograft reconstruction have been found to be similar in patient-reported outcomes",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
